.TH SWIFTJLS-CLI 1 "October 10, 2026" "1.1.0-dev.2" "Swift Image Compression Suite"
.SH NAME
swiftjls-cli \- native scalar JPEG-LS codec
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swiftjls-cli
.RI [ options ] " command " [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Native scalar lossless and near-lossless JPEG-LS for unsigned greyscale.
The library supports 2 through 16 meaningful bits in 16-bit storage.
Build with Swift 6.2 or newer in Swift 6 language mode. Apple OS minimum is
26.0.
CLI hosts are macOS and Linux; consult qualification records for executed
coverage.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B capabilities [\-\-json]
Report actual library encode/decode/inspect support. JSON is one document on
stdout.
False support values and empty formats mean unavailable algorithms.
.TP
.B help [command]
Show global or command-specific help. No arguments also show global help.
.TP
.B version
Show the development version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help, including after a command.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the development version.
.TP
.B \-v, \-vv, \-vvv, \-vvvv, \-vvvvv
Increase diagnostic verbosity, up to 5.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose LEVEL, \-\-verbose=LEVEL
Set level to 1 through 5, or + through +++++. Bare verbose increments once.
.TP
.B \-verbose: LEVEL, \-verbose:LEVEL
Equivalent explicit verbosity spelling; bare \-verbose increments once.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress optional diagnostics; errors remain visible. Conflicts with
verbosity.
.SH DIAGNOSTIC LEVELS
Default 0 reports errors only. Levels are cumulative:
1 summary; 2 stages; 3 capability/configuration details; 4 elapsed timing;
5 bounded trace. Invalid levels or totals above 5 return 2.
Explicit levels set and repeated flags increment in argument order.
Diagnostics use stderr. Requested help/version/capability data uses stdout.
No payload bytes, metadata, raw addresses or input/output paths are logged.
.SH CODEC COMMANDS
encode reads attached raw 2D uint16 NRRD and writes JPEG-LS.
decode reads JPEG-LS and writes NRRD, requiring 16 meaningful bits.
inspect checks headers and reports dimensions and precision.
validate also decodes the complete sample payload.
.PP
Use \-i/\-\-input and \-o/\-\-output for files or a single hyphen for streams.
Input/output formats are nrrd and jls as applicable to the command.
Use \-\-mode lossless (default) or near-lossless with \-\-max-error 1 through
255.
The scalar backend uses one worker; \-\-threads is a ceiling.
Copy policy is require-sharing by default; allow-copy is also accepted.
Use \-\-max-memory BYTES and \-\-timeout SECONDS to set finite limits.
Defaults are 1 GiB and 120 seconds. Both must be positive.
.PP
Existing output is refused unless \-\-overwrite is supplied.
Files use a sibling transaction and atomic publication; incomplete files are
removed.
Binary stdout cannot be rolled back. A failed stream may contain partial
bytes.
JSON inspect/validate output uses stdout; encode/decode JSON reports use
stderr.
Pipe serialisation involves copies, independently of in-process shared
storage.
.PP
The NRRD profile requires explicit endian and permits no detached references,
compression, colour, signed samples or ancillary interpretation fields.
Lower meaningful precision cannot be silently widened for NRRD output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success/help/version; 2 invalid usage; 3 malformed input;
4 unsupported format/feature/layout/backend; 5 resource/deadline;
6 I/O failure including a closed pipe; 7 internal failure; 130 cancellation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
swiftjls-cli \-h
swiftjls-cli help capabilities
swiftjls-cli capabilities \-\-json \-vv
swiftjls-cli capabilities \-verbose: 3
swiftjls-cli capabilities \-\-verbose=+++++
.fi
.SH INSTALLATION
Scripts/install-cli.sh installs or updates the executable and this page
together.
Use \-\-prefix for an absolute prefix (default /usr/local), \-\-destdir or
DESTDIR
for staging, and \-\-binary for a prebuilt binary matching VERSION.
Files are PREFIX/bin/swiftjls-cli and PREFIX/share/man/man1/swiftjls-cli.1.
For custom prefixes use man \-M PREFIX/share/man swiftjls-cli, or configure
MANPATH.
No index refresh is needed for direct lookup; no sudo runs automatically.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1)
.PP
CLI.md and Documentation/Engineering/CodecMigration/README.md in the SwiftJLS
repository.
